1312..1383 Comment "/// Spinning a sum is composing the spins (cubical\'s `intLoop-hom`), by"
1384..1457 Comment "/// induction on the second summand. `spin` puts its new loop first where"
1458..1535 Comment "/// cubical\'s `intLoop` puts it last, so the law composes the spins the other"
1536..1602 Comment "/// way round, as the words compute: `Path.step(loop ∷ p, q)` is"
1603..1686 Comment "/// `loop ∷ Path.step(p, q)` (#422). At zero `spin(Z)` is a call that returns the"
1687..1761 Comment "/// empty word, and the composite over it runs that call first (#473); the"
1762..1833 Comment "/// composites the arms carry convert through their definitions (#440)."
